# sweep: --bare --seed-root apps/homepanel/fixtures/tiles
# A panel with twelve saved tiles and readings from an earlier poll, on a
# reader whose token is missing, so every request fails the same way.
wait-for kitchen · on
# Readings from another day say which day.
expect Offline since 1 Sep at 06:40. Readings may be stale.
expect Showing readings from 1 Sep at 06:40.
expect living room · 20.5°
expect humidity · 48 %
clean
shot homepanel-tiles
# A light toggles through Home Assistant. When that fails the tile keeps
# its last reading and the banner names the tile.
tap kitchen · on
wait-for Couldn't update kitchen.
expect kitchen · on
clean
shot homepanel-toggle-failed
# A sensor only shows its reading.
tap outdoor temperature
wait-for This tile only shows its reading.
expect State: 12.5 °C
expect sensor.outdoor_temperature
clean
shot homepanel-reading
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for kitchen · on
# A thermostat opens its own screen with the room and target temperature.
tap living room
wait-for Target: 21°
expect Room: 20.5°
expect State: heat
expect Cooler
expect Power
clean
shot homepanel-climate
tap Warmer
wait-for Couldn't set the temperature.
expect Target: 21°
tap Cooler
wait-for Couldn't set the temperature.
tap Power
wait-for Couldn't update living room.
clean
shot homepanel-climate-failed
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for kitchen · on
# Twelve is the limit, and Add says so instead of opening the picker.
tap Add tile
wait-for Home Panel can show up to 12 tiles.
expect-missing Finding devices
clean
shot homepanel-tile-limit
# Settings counts the tiles. Edit tiles lists them six to a page.
tap Settings
wait-for 12 of 12
# The grid's banners stay on the grid.
expect-missing Home Panel can show up to 12 tiles.
expect-missing No Home Assistant account
tap Edit tiles
wait-for front door
expect More tiles (1/2)
expect-missing porch
clean
shot homepanel-edit-page-one
tap More tiles (1/2)
wait-for porch
expect More tiles (2/2)
expect-missing front door
# Move up swaps a tile with the one before it, in the list and on the grid.
tap heater
wait-for switch.heater
expect State: off
expect Move up
clean
shot homepanel-tile-screen
tap Move up
wait-for More tiles (2/2)
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Wall panel
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for heater · off
# Remove takes the tile off; the first tile has no Move up. The note says
# which tile went, and the grid's outage is not repeated here.
tap Settings
wait-for 12 of 12
tap Edit tiles
wait-for kitchen
tap kitchen
wait-for light.kitchen
expect-missing Move up
tap Remove
wait-for kitchen removed.
expect coffee maker
expect-missing light.kitchen
expect-missing No Home Assistant account
clean
shot homepanel-removed
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for 11 of 12
# Both changes survive a restart.
restart
wait-for coffee maker · off
expect-missing kitchen · on
tap Settings
wait-for 11 of 12
tap Edit tiles
wait-for coffee maker
tap More tiles (1/2)
wait-for heater
tap-id 4294967295
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for coffee maker · off
# With room again, Add asks Home Assistant for its devices and says why
# it could not get them. The picker stays open on adding a device by its ID.
tap Add tile
wait-for No Home Assistant account is on this reader yet
expect Add a device by its ID
clean
shot homepanel-add-failed
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for coffee maker · off
# With a token on the reader, a reader off Wi-Fi says so, and a Home
# Assistant that does not answer is told apart from it.
companion secret set homeassistant --from apps/homepanel/fixtures/token --sim
scenario offline
tap heater
wait-for Couldn't update heater. This reader is not on Wi-Fi.
expect heater · off
clean
shot homepanel-offline
scenario host-down
tap heater
wait-for Couldn't update heater. Home Assistant did not answer
clean
shot homepanel-host-down
